{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25616890",
      "title": "Using Fallback Pages & Re-deploying",
      "sourceHash": "c2c5bc0fe8c7ade4e97d434c812edd3c66869210404619807ad851adbcdba70e",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.02,
          "end": 4.39,
          "en": "The problem here is that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.39,
          "end": 6.62,
          "en": "on the single meetup page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.62,
          "end": 11.62,
          "en": "we do specify which meetup pages should be pre-generated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.72,
          "end": 16.6,
          "en": "and we only set this at build time and never thereafter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.6,
          "end": 19.11,
          "en": "And since we set fallback to false,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.11,
          "end": 23.19,
          "en": "we also ensure that any requests to meetups,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23.19,
          "end": 26.33,
          "en": "for which no page was pre-generated before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.33,
          "end": 28,
          "en": "will fail.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28,
          "end": 31.29,
          "en": "Now that worked as long as we didn't add a new meetup,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.29,
          "end": 33.01,
          "en": "and it worked during development,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.01,
          "end": 36.63,
          "en": "because there the getStaticPaths function ran",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.63,
          "end": 38.4,
          "en": "for every incoming request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.4,
          "end": 40.823,
          "en": "but it now fails after deployment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.8,
          "end": 45.95,
          "en": "Now fixing it is quite simple though, thankfully.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.95,
          "end": 50.95,
          "en": "We can set fallback to true, or even better, to 'blocking'.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.14,
          "end": 54.63,
          "en": "When you set fallback to true or to blocking,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.63,
          "end": 58.84,
          "en": "you're telling NextJS that the list of paths",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.84,
          "end": 62.94,
          "en": "which you're specifying here, might not be exhaustive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.94,
          "end": 65.68,
          "en": "there might be more valid pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 65.68,
          "end": 70.68,
          "en": "And, therefore, when fallback is set to true or to blocking,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 70.82,
          "end": 75.68,
          "en": "NextJS will not respond with a 404 page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 75.68,
          "end": 78.82,
          "en": "if it can't find the page immediately.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 78.82,
          "end": 82.38,
          "en": "Instead with fallback set to true or blocking,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 82.38,
          "end": 85.03,
          "en": "it will then generate that page on demand,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 85.03,
          "end": 86.75,
          "en": "and thereafter cache it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 86.75,
          "end": 90.49,
          "en": "so it will pre-generate it when needed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 90.49,
          "end": 93.95,
          "en": "Now the difference between true and blocking then is that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 93.95,
          "end": 98.17,
          "en": "with true, it would immediately return an empty page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 98.17,
          "end": 102.61,
          "en": "and then pull down the dynamically generated content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 102.61,
          "end": 103.99000000000001,
          "en": "once that's done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 103.99000000000001,
          "end": 106.25,
          "en": "So you need to handle that case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 106.25,
          "end": 109.44,
          "en": "that the page does not have the data yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 109.44,
          "end": 112.84,
          "en": "With blocking, the user will not see anything until",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 112.84,
          "end": 114.86,
          "en": "the page was pre-generated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 114.86,
          "end": 117.32,
          "en": "and the finished page will be served.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 117.32,
          "end": 119.27000000000001,
          "en": "And that's the approach I will use here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 119.27000000000001,
          "end": 124.22,
          "en": "since it doesn't require any other extra work from our side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 124.22,
          "end": 126.58,
          "en": "So if we change fallback to blocking,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 126.58,
          "end": 129.4,
          "en": "we'll not face this problem anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 129.4,
          "end": 131.91,
          "en": "Now we just need to redeploy this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 131.91,
          "end": 134.71,
          "en": "And for this, all we have to do is create",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 134.71,
          "end": 138.05,
          "en": "a new code snapshot with git add,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 138.05,
          "end": 139.73,
          "en": "and then with git commit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 139.73,
          "end": 144.123,
          "en": "where we say, \"fixed fallback\", or something like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 145.06,
          "end": 148.42000000000002,
          "en": "and then simply push our branch again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 148.42000000000002,
          "end": 152.61,
          "en": "push our repository back onto GitHub.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 152.61,
          "end": 157.41,
          "en": "And the great thing is that NextJS will actually watch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 157.41,
          "end": 160.14,
          "en": "this main branch to which we pushed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 160.14,
          "end": 162.45,
          "en": "and whenever it detects a change there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 162.45,
          "end": 165.78,
          "en": "it will automatically start building and redeploying.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 165.78,
          "end": 168.97,
          "en": "As you can see here, it's building already again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 168.97,
          "end": 170.34,
          "en": "So that's very convenient.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 170.34,
          "end": 173.23,
          "en": "If you want to update your page and redeploy,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 173.23,
          "end": 176.94,
          "en": "all you have to do is create a new commit and push it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 176.94,
          "end": 179.223,
          "en": "to your connected GitHub repository,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 180.35,
          "end": 184.33,
          "en": "and that will then automatically trigger a redeployment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 184.33,
          "end": 185.75,
          "en": "And whilst it's redeploying,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 185.75,
          "end": 188.06,
          "en": "your old page will stay up and running.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 188.06,
          "end": 191.6,
          "en": "But once it's done, the new page will take over,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 191.6,
          "end": 194.25,
          "en": "and hence, now this meetup exists here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 194.25,
          "end": 198.79,
          "en": "And if we add another meetup here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 198.79,
          "end": 203.79,
          "en": "with this image, and our test address, and some test text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 204.25,
          "end": 209.25,
          "en": "If we do this, now our change should also be in effect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 209.91,
          "end": 212.59,
          "en": "And if we now reload the starting page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 212.59,
          "end": 214.81,
          "en": "a couple of times to revalidate it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 214.81,
          "end": 216.36,
          "en": "if we now visit this meetup,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 216.36,
          "end": 220.23,
          "en": "it's created on the fly and does all the works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 220.23,
          "end": 223.24,
          "en": "And that is also something, which I wanted to show you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 223.24,
          "end": 226.95,
          "en": "especially combined with that redeployment feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 226.95,
          "end": 229.65,
          "en": "which is also something you should know.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 229.65,
          "end": 231.5,
          "en": "Now, there is, of course, more you can do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 231.5,
          "end": 233.45,
          "en": "You can connect a custom domain here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 233.45,
          "end": 236.44,
          "en": "and you can also configure more in your project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 236.44,
          "end": 239.19,
          "en": "There are more features, which you can add as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 239.19,
          "end": 241.04,
          "en": "but I mentioned this before already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 241.04,
          "end": 243.92,
          "en": "There are simply more things, which you could add.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 243.92,
          "end": 246.28,
          "en": "This tutorial, however, had the goal of giving you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 246.28,
          "end": 249.312,
          "en": "an overview of the most important features and,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 249.312,
          "end": 251.403,
          "en": "therefore, we're now finished with that.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}